[h1]Phobos Shipbreaker[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.28.1
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

Make the wreck pay for the next repair. Rivetline equipment brings wall processing, scrap recovery and aluminium casting aboard your ship.

[h2]What it does[/h2]
[list]
[*]Feed detached ordinary walls through G4 and H4 into D4, or use the local manual feed.
[*]R4 recovers steel and aluminium from identified R2 panel residue. Rejects remain aboard; running them again yields nothing.
[*]C2 collects supported residue and products. Link receivers and start transfers separately from processing.
[*]F6 casts aluminium housings using electricity and one cooling assembly. Hot metal and gas stay sealed until safe release.
[*]Choose direct cooling or F6-C pipes to an exterior radiator. Optional coolant servicing uses separate industrial fluid.
[*]Prepare an owned, empty, depressurized target for G4 capture and powered ordinary-wall cutting. Recover valuables and crew first.
[*]Use the C1 console for equipment on your own ship, or work beside each machine. Crew orders can supply and run permitted jobs.
[/list]

[h2]Operating limits[/h2]
Keep the supporting hull walls under the sealed chute. Processing needs power, output space and suitable cooling; vacuum is not free cooling. Older unclassified residue has no R4 recipe. Furnace heating and exterior work pause on interruption and require Resume. Capture does not by itself authorize cutting. Loading preserves cargo and work; a fault may block further work for inspection.

[h2]Requirements and installation[/h2]
Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5, Phobos Framework 0.28.0 or newer and Phobos Auto Nav 0.19.0 or newer. Crafting Framework and Salvage Workshop are optional. Agriculture integration is optional.

This is an unpublished development package. Automated checks do not establish in-game readiness or Unity layout approval. Keep required mods installed for saves using their content. Updating does not refill shops or old loot containers. See the installation guide for current download availability.

[h2]English wording update[/h2]
Controls, warnings and descriptions use clearer language. Equipment identities, saved progress, recipes and gameplay values are unchanged.

[h2]Guides, sources and credits[/h2]
Created by Phobos A. D'thorga (phobosgekko). Independent community work, not endorsed by Blue Bottle Games, Kitfox Games or the research institutions cited below. Research informs design; compact equipment, yields and operating limits remain gameplay choices.
The linked guides preserve Blue Bottle Games game evidence and the original research authors beside their claims. Valtora owns the optional Ship's Water integration. LOGUSS's Common Sense modules and jossla's Study at Terminals retain their own work and attribution.
Original artwork uses AI-assisted production; artwork provenance and licensing are recorded separately.

